<title>USA: RAC Financial Group Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>RAC Financial Group Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>		   Three Months Ended December 31,</p>
<p>					     1996	     1995 REVENUES:</p>
<p>   Gain on sales of loans, net $  95,848     $  20,273</p>
<p>   Interest			     20,432	   1,767</p>
<p>   Servicing income		    2,908	     694</p>
<p>   Other income			  4,400	     734</p>
<p>		Total revenues	 123,588	  23,468</p>
<p>EXPENSES</p>
<p>   Salaries and employee benefits 14,838	   5.459</p>
<p>   Interest			     13,132	   2,043</p>
<p>   Other operating		    21,048	   3,761</p>
<p>Provision for possible</p>
<p>    credit losses		     44,388	   4,649</p>
<p>		Total expenses	  93,406	  15,912</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	 30,182	   7,556</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes     (11,469)	 (2,871)</p>
<p>   Net income			   18,713	   4,685</p>
<p>   Average shares		     29,033	  20,297</p>
<p>Primary net income per share</p>
<p>     of common stock		    0.64	    0.23</p>
<p>   Average shares		     34,957	  20,297</p>
<p>Fully diluted net income per</p>
<p>     share of common stock	    0.57	    0.23</p>
<p>NOTES: Per share calculated to include two-for-one stock split on November 29, 1996.</p>
<p>One-time after tax charges during the quarter included $1.1 million or $0.03 per share to induce convertible note holders to convert into common shares about 33 months before call date.  </p>
<p>Also included $620,000 or $0.02 per share to cover certain costs for expected relocation of company headquarters in Dallas.</p>
</text>
